From 41b11cf87c50e9ae49c70bc669c6c7c29a6569c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] review_independence: let a card's own worker shell
 complete via the CLI

A dispatched worker's terminal shell carries HERMES_KANBAN_WORKER_TASK and
HERMES_SESSION_ID, not HERMES_KANBAN_TASK/HERMES_KANBAN_RUN_ID, so a reviewer
that fell back to `hermes kanban complete` (kanban-worker CLI fallback on tool
DB errors) was refused as an outside caller and told to "leave the card for a
worker". Its completion closes the card's own claimed run, whose owner_admitted
session is the reviewer's: ship's _review_verdict accepts that record (probed
against ~/.hermes/lib/core-tools/hermes-core-wt-land).

kanban_worker_shell.run_for proves the run instead of trusting the env var:
the card is running under a claim with an open current run, this process
descends from that run's live worker_bound interpreter (or fingerprinted
spawn pid; never pid 1), and HERMES_SESSION_ID equals the run's single
admitted session. The proven run id is passed as expected_run_id, so the
write is fenced to that run. When the env names the card but the proof fails,
the refusal now says the CLI fallback cannot record a review ship accepts and
to retry the tool or kanban_block. A card that only names a core pull (no
stated contract) is described as such (review nit 1 on #1667).
